        "original_id": "d60a466f-c649-5e34-b87c-fdc4c9e32b3f",
        "text": "This chunk is about:\n- People: Briana Corrigan, Dave Hemingway, Hugh Whitaker\n- Songs: \"A Little Time\", \"Five Get Over Excited\"\n- Albums: Choke\n- Bands: The Beautiful South, The South\n- Topics: chart performance, band lineup changes, promotional videos\n\nFacts:\n- Briana Corrigan was born on 30 May 1965 and is a Northern Irish singer.\n- \"A Little Time\" consists of a duet featuring vocalists Dave Hemingway and Briana Corrigan.\n- The South's album Choke was pushed to number 2 in the charts after the release of the band's first and only number 1 single, \"A Little Time\".\n- Hugh Whitaker left the band on amicable terms and appeared in the promotional video for \"Five Get Over Excited\".\n- In the promotional video for \"Five Get Over Excited\", Hugh Whitaker was depicted as being kidnapped by his replacement, Dave Hemingway, and locked in a hessian sack.",
